---
// Goal: Select OpenRouter and check its System One route.
import SidePage from '../../../layouts/SidePage.astro';
import BackendFacts from '../../../components/BackendFacts.astro';
import CheckLines from '../../../components/CheckLines.astro';
import { BACKEND_PAGES } from '../../../data/catalog.mjs';
import { backend } from '../../../lib/backends-table.mjs';
const b = backend('openrouter');
const page = BACKEND_PAGES.find((p) => p.slug === b.name);
---
<SidePage pages={BACKEND_PAGES} page={{ ...page, description: 'OpenRouter through ThinkThen: address, model, key variable and check.' }} name="Backends">
  <h1>OpenRouter</h1>
  <p class="lede">Select this backend with <code>--backend {b.name}</code>.</p>
  <BackendFacts name={b.name} />
  <p>Put your provider key in <code>{b.keys[0]}</code>. ThinkThen reads this variable when you select the backend.</p>
  <h2>Check the connection</h2>
  <p>Run <code>thinkthen backends check --backend {b.name} --timeout 90</code>. A run with <code>--plan</code> needs no key and sends nothing.</p>
  <CheckLines name={b.name} />
  <p>The 2026-10-04 check asked <code>typesafe/jev-1.13</code>; all four successful replies named <code>typesafe/jev-1.13-20260917</code>. This check establishes no result for other models or routes.</p>
  <p>OpenRouter requires both sides when a yes-or-no question has criteria. ThinkThen preserves your descriptions and sends an empty object for a missing side. Questions without descriptions omit criteria.</p>
  <p>The <a href="https://openrouter.ai/typesafe/jev-1.13">provider documentation</a> was checked on 2026-10-04. Read the provider's terms before sending sensitive text.</p>
  <h2>Clef and Clef-flash</h2>
  <p>Choose the measured text model with <code>--backend openrouter --model cloudflare/clef</code> or <code>--backend openrouter --model cloudflare/clef-flash</code>. On 2026-10-05, experiment 0034 passed each model's 15-request text check with no critical findings or warnings. This proves those inputs and routes, not accuracy. The <a href="https://github.com/botassembly/thinkthen-exp/tree/d628a91687f7a020160fae9a75e4c65fdd3edeff/experiments/0034-images-across-decision-models">recorded report</a> retains the exchanges and controls.</p>
  <p>The retained model metadata lists a 65,536-token context, while the model pages warn of roughly 2K text-state truncation. Recorded input tariffs were $0.24 per million for Clef and $0.09 for Clef-flash, with free output. These observations are dated 2026-10-05.</p>
  <p>The tested decision route shows no observable image use: Earth, no image and a shuttle returned identical typed answers and full distributions on both models, with zero deltas in all 18 pairwise comparisons. Image understanding on this route is unsupported for product claims. Accepted data URLs alone prove no image use, size limit or accuracy. Development 0.2 continues to refuse images on this OpenRouter route.</p>
  <p>Direct Cloudflare Workers AI remains unverified. Its vendor route is <code>https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/&#123;ACCOUNT_ID&#125;/ai/run/@cf/cloudflare/clef</code>, or the corresponding <code>clef-flash</code> path; vendor examples use <code>CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN</code>. No run here establishes that reply envelope as a ThinkThen System One reply. The retained direct input prices are $0.24/M and $0.09/M; the direct output tariff remains unknown. The vendor's documented PNG/JPEG/WebP and four-image allowance establishes no ThinkThen direct-route support.</p>

  <h2>Price and limits</h2>
  <p>On 2026-10-04, <a href="https://openrouter.ai/typesafe/jev-1.13">OpenRouter's Jev 1.13 page</a> listed $0.042 per million input tokens, free output and a 32,000-token context window. ThinkThen's own request limits still apply.</p>
  <p>The backend paces nothing unless the configuration file sets <code>requests_per_minute</code>. That rate applies to one process. Concurrent processes each get their own rate.</p>
  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/install/backends/">All backends</a> · <a href="/install/configuration/">Configuration</a></p>
</SidePage>

<style>
  p code { white-space: normal; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
